  "note": "Endings-only unit split out of a1_prep_do_z (2026-08-02, load). Regular Gen sg by gender: m -u, n -a, f -y. Uzycie = duzo/blisko + Gen sentences (governors that need no case elsewhere). No do/z here; do/z next unit rides these forms. k/g-stem fem (-i) and masc animate (-a) deferred.",
  "focus_structures": [
    "gen_endings"
  ],
  "intro": [
    {
      "title": "One new ending per gender",
      "title_pl": "Jedna końcówka na rodzaj",
      "body": "The next units use the prepositions do (to) and z (from). Both change the noun's ending — the new form is called the genitive (dopełniacz).\n\nGood news: for the words you know, the ending follows the gender you can already spot. One rule per gender:",
      "body_pl": "Do i z zmieniają końcówkę rzeczownika — to dopełniacz. Jedna reguła na rodzaj:",
      "table": {
        "headers": [
          "Gender",
          "Rule",
          "Examples"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "m. (masculine thing)",
            "add -u",
            "dom → domu · sklep → sklepu · telefon → telefonu"
          ],
          [
            "n. (neuter, -o)",
            "-o → -a",
            "miasto → miasta · mleko → mleka · piwo → piwa"
          ],
          [
            "ż. (feminine, -a)",
            "-a → -y",
            "szkoła → szkoły · kawa → kawy · woda → wody"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Careful: this is not the locative",
      "title_pl": "Uwaga: to nie miejscownik",
      "body": "You just learned w sklepie (in the shop). Sklepu is a DIFFERENT form with a different job — sklepie says where you are, sklepu will say where you're going to or from (next unit).\n\nHere, just learn the endings. No sentences yet.",
      "body_pl": "Sklepie (miejscownik) ≠ sklepu (dopełniacz). Tu tylko końcówki, bez zdań.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "house/home → ",
          "pl": "dom → domu"
        },
        {
          "en": "city →",
          "pl": "miasto → miasta"
        },
        {
          "en": "school →",
          "pl": "szkoła → szkoły"
        },
        {
          "en": "coffee →",
          "pl": "kawa → kawy"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Two words that take the genitive",
      "title_pl": "Dwa słówka z dopełniaczem",
      "body": "You can already use these endings in real sentences — with two new words:\n\ndużo + Gen = a lot of... → dużo kawy, dużo wody, dużo mleka\nblisko + Gen = near... → blisko domu, blisko sklepu, blisko szkoły\n\nMam dużo kawy. · Piję dużo wody. · Mieszkam blisko sklepu.",
      "body_pl": "dużo + dopełniacz (dużo kawy) · blisko + dopełniacz (blisko domu).",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "I have a lot of coffee.",
          "pl": "Mam dużo kawy."
        },
        {
          "en": "I drink a lot of water.",
          "pl": "Piję dużo wody."
        },
        {
          "en": "I live near the shop.",
          "pl": "Mieszkam blisko sklepu."
        },
        {
          "en": "I'm near home.",
          "pl": "Jestem blisko domu."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
